---
/** "We'll check this claim:" — the most important addition in the flow.
 *
 *  Before this step, submitting a URL silently sent up to 4,000 characters of
 *  article body as "the claim", and the reader never saw what the system
 *  thought it was checking. Showing the extracted claim back converts an
 *  unanswerable question into an answerable one and makes our interpretation
 *  auditable by the person who asked (NEWZWALE_UI_UX_SPEC §5.2).
 *
 *  Shown when the input is a URL or a long paragraph. A short typed claim is
 *  already its own confirmation, so it goes straight through.
 */
---

<div id="claim-confirm-step" hidden class="flex flex-col gap-3">
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">We'll check this claim</h2>

  <p class="text-sm text-body">
    This is what we extracted from what you pasted. Correct it if it is not the claim you meant.
  </p>

  <blockquote
    class="rounded-sm border border-hairline bg-surface-elevated px-4 py-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink"
  >
    <span id="claim-confirm-text"></span>
  </blockquote>

  <p id="claim-confirm-origin" hidden class="font-mono-caption text-mute">
    Extracted from <span id="claim-confirm-origin-host"></span>
  </p>

  <label for="claim-confirm-edit" class="sr-only">Edit the claim before checking</label>
  <textarea
    id="claim-confirm-edit"
    hidden
    rows="3"
    maxlength="2000"
    class="w-full resize-y rounded-sm border border-hairline bg-surface-elevated px-4 py-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink focus:outline-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary-strong"
  ></textarea>

  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
    <button
      type="button"
      id="claim-confirm-go"
      class="btn-pill-primary inline-flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center px-5 text-sm"
    >
      Check this
    </button>
    <button
      type="button"
      id="claim-confirm-edit-btn"
      class="btn-pill-secondary inline-flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center px-5 text-sm"
    >
      Edit
    </button>
    <button
      type="button"
      id="claim-confirm-back"
      class="inline-flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center px-2 text-sm font-semibold text-primary-strong"
    >
      Start over
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
